# Build context control.
#
# Without this file the context is ~1.8 GB -- .venv at 1.1 GB and data/ at 740 MB, of which
# 324 MB is the DuckDB warehouse. All of it is uploaded to the builder before the first
# instruction runs. On a hosted builder that is the difference between a deploy and a
# timeout.
#
# The Dockerfile copies four things: pyproject.toml, README.md, src/, and (added for the
# release command) alembic.ini + migrations/. Everything else is context the build never
# reads.

# --- The two that matter ---------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Raw M5 extracts, the derived warehouse, and users' uploaded history. Nothing in the
# deployed service reads any of it: tier 2 works on what the user uploads at runtime, and
# the dashboard's tier 1 figures are inlined as JSON at build time by
# scripts/build_dashboard.py. The 324 MB warehouse would otherwise be shipped for nothing.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so it means the *repository's* data/ and nothing else. The
# festival demand table now lives at src/inventory_engine/data/ -- it is package data that
# ships with the wheel -- and excluding it broke every forecast in the first deployment.
# The negation below is belt and braces against an implementation that matches nested
# directories.
/data/
!src/inventory_engine/data/

# --- VCS and CI ------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# --- Python build and test residue -----------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.log

# --- Experiment tracking ---------------------------------------------------------------
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# --- Agent tooling and planning artefacts, not application source -----------------------
.claude/
_bmad/
_bmad-output/
design-artifacts/
wds-0-project-setup/
wds-1-project-brief/
wds-2-requirements-analysis/

# --- Not copied by the Dockerfile ------------------------------------------------------
# The suite does not run inside the image; CI runs it on the runner. Remove this line if
# that ever changes.
tests/
# The dashboard is a static page deployed separately; the service mounts no static files.
dashboard/
node_modules/
# Documentation is read on GitHub, not served by the container.
docs/
scripts/
migrations/versions/__pycache__/

# --- Editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# --- Local env; secrets come from `fly secrets`, never from the image -------------------
.env
.env.*
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
